  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1018 PM MDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nDrier southwesterly flow will gradually transition to more \nzonal flow by Wednesday as high pressure builds into the Desert \nSouthwest. As a result, generally clear skies and warming \ntemperatures will be the story for the coming week. There is a \nlow (<15%) chance for an isolated shower or thunderstorm over \nthe San Juans and Divide each afternoon. Temperatures will run \n5-10 degrees above normal through the rest of the work week, \nwith potential to drop back to near normal values over the \nweekend. Guidance is hinting at a potential moisture return at \nthat point, as a trough moves into the Pacific Northwest and \npushes the high to the east. However, agreement on this solution\nis still somewhat poor, so stay tuned if you have plans this \ncoming weekend. In the meantime, enjoy the pleasant late \nsummer/early fall conditions.",
